{#
  DateTimePicker macro — text field + icon button opening a WAI-ARIA APG
  Date Picker Dialog (month grid, optional time selects).

  HTML tag: <div> (root), <input>+<button> (field), <div role="dialog"> (popup)
  CSS class: date-time-picker
  Companion runtime: date-time-picker.client.js

  This is the FIFTH helper in the catalog and the hardest port: unlike the
  three *-select helpers (a static option list) and share-picker (real,
  final <a href> links), a calendar's grid, weekday headers, period
  heading and hour/minute option lists cannot be produced by a template
  at all — they need Intl.DateTimeFormat and civil-date arithmetic that
  Nunjucks has no access to. So this macro renders every piece of markup
  whose text is FIXED at render time (the trigger, the header nav
  buttons, the footer, any shortcut buttons, the hour/minute <label>s)
  and leaves the Intl-dependent interior — the weekday <th> row, the
  <tbody> of day cells, the period heading text, the hour/minute
  <option> lists, and the meridiem select itself — for
  date-time-picker.client.js to build the first time it runs. See
  spec/index.md §3.4 for the full account, and §4.3 for exactly what
  each side owns.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  NUNJUCKS DEVIATIONS from the canonical Svelte props
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------

  1. isDateDisabled: (isoDate) => boolean  in Svelte.
     A macro cannot evaluate a predicate, and the calendar it would
     gate is not rendered here at all (see above) — so there is
     nothing to apply it to at render time. The macro instead accepts
     `disabledDates`, an array of ISO date strings, emitted as a JSON
     data attribute. date-time-picker.client.js reads it as the
     baseline disabled set on every root — including one hydrated with
     no custom JavaScript at all — and a real `isDateDisabled` function
     passed to `initDateTimePicker` layers on top of it (or replaces it)
     for rules a finite list cannot express, e.g. "no weekends".
     See spec/index.md §3.4.

  2. formatValue / parseInput / onChange / onShortcut / onInvalidInput:
     all functions in Svelte. These have no template equivalent to
     deviate INTO — they are client-only concerns and pass straight
     through as `initDateTimePicker(root, {formatValue, parseInput,
     onChange, onShortcut, onInvalidInput})` options with no macro-side
     substitute needed at all.

  3. hour12: in Svelte this resolves from `locale` via Intl when unset.
     A macro cannot call Intl, so it cannot decide whether the
     meridiem select should exist. The macro therefore never renders
     it; date-time-picker.client.js resolves `hour12` (from the opt,
     the data attribute, or the locale) and creates the meridiem
     <label>+<select> itself, only when the clock turns out to be
     12-hour. Its label comes from `labels.meridiem`, forwarded as a
     data attribute since the element it names does not exist yet.

  4. shortcuts: plain data (id/label/days/months/date, no functions),
     so — unlike 1–3 — there is NO deviation here. The macro renders
     each shortcut as a real button up front, exactly as it would any
     other static list. A consumer building a root with no macro may
     still pass `shortcuts` to `initDateTimePicker`, which then owns
     the container instead of the pre-rendered buttons (client wins,
     matching share-picker's function-href precedent).

  Params (single `opts` object):
    label          — string, required. Names the trigger AND the dialog.
    labels         — object, required. previousYear/previousMonth/
                     nextMonth/nextYear/confirm/cancel are required;
                     hour/minute are required when mode includes a time;
                     meridiem is required when a 12-hour clock is used;
                     week is required when showWeekNumbers; clear is
                     optional and gates the clear button.
    mode           — "date" | "time" | "datetime", default "date".
    value          — string. Initial ISO value (YYYY-MM-DD / HH:MM /
                     YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM per mode). Shown RAW in the text
                     field until the client reformats it — the macro
                     cannot call Intl. See spec/index.md §5.7.
    locale         — string. BCP 47 tag. Forwarded as a data attribute;
                     init opts win.
    min / max      — string. Inclusive ISO date bounds.
    disabledDates  — array of ISO date strings. See deviation 1 above.
    firstDayOfWeek — number, 0 = Sunday … 6 = Saturday.
    minuteStep     — number, default 1.
    hour12         — boolean. See deviation 3 above.
    showWeekNumbers— boolean.
    shortcuts      — array of {id, label, days?, months?, date?}. See 4.
    confirmOnSelect— boolean. Default (mode === "date") is resolved on
                     the client, since the macro has no other default
                     mechanism worth adding for one boolean.
    name           — string, default "date-time". Discriminator for ids.
    id             — string, default "date-time-picker-{name}".
    inputId        — string. Overrides the text field's id.
    describedBy    — string. Forwarded as aria-describedby.
    placeholder    — string.
    disabled / readonly / required — boolean.
    classes        — string. Extra CSS classes on the root.
    attributes     — object. Extra HTML attributes spread onto the root.

    {% call %} body replaces the default calendar glyph inside the
    button, exactly like share-picker's glyph override.

  Usage:
    {% from "./date-time-picker.njk" import dateTimePicker %}
    {{ dateTimePicker({
      label: "Appointment date",
      labels: {
        previousYear: "Previous year", previousMonth: "Previous month",
        nextMonth: "Next month", nextYear: "Next year",
        confirm: "Confirm", cancel: "Cancel", clear: "Clear"
      },
      mode: "date",
      value: appointment.date,
      min: "2026-01-01"
    }) }}

  Then load date-time-picker.client.js once and call autoInit().

  Spec: spec/index.md §4.1 (macro parameters), §4.3 (DOM contract).
#}
{%- macro dateTimePicker(opts) -%}
{%- set name = opts.name | default("date-time") -%}
{%- set id = opts.id | default("date-time-picker-" + name) -%}
{%- set dialogId = id + "-dialog" -%}
{%- set periodId = id + "-period" -%}
{%- set fieldId = opts.inputId | default(id + "-input") -%}
{%- set hourId = id + "-hour" -%}
{%- set minuteId = id + "-minute" -%}
{%- set mode = opts.mode | default("date") -%}
{%- set labels = opts.labels | default({}) -%}
{%- set usesDate = mode !== "time" -%}
{%- set usesTime = mode !== "date" -%}
{%- set showWeekNumbers = opts.showWeekNumbers | default(false) -%}
{%- set shortcuts = opts.shortcuts | default([]) -%}
<div
  class="date-time-picker{% if opts.classes %} {{ opts.classes }}{% endif %}"
  data-lily-date-time-picker-root
  data-mode="{{ mode }}"
  data-lily-date-time-picker-name="{{ name }}"
  {%- if opts.locale %} data-lily-date-time-picker-locale="{{ opts.locale }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.min %} data-lily-date-time-picker-min="{{ opts.min }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.max %} data-lily-date-time-picker-max="{{ opts.max }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.disabledDates %} data-lily-date-time-picker-disabled-dates="{{ opts.disabledDates | dump }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.firstDayOfWeek is defined %} data-lily-date-time-picker-first-day-of-week="{{ opts.firstDayOfWeek }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.minuteStep is defined %} data-lily-date-time-picker-minute-step="{{ opts.minuteStep }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.hour12 is defined %} data-lily-date-time-picker-hour12="{{ opts.hour12 }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if showWeekNumbers %} data-lily-date-time-picker-show-week-numbers="true"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.confirmOnSelect is defined %} data-lily-date-time-picker-confirm-on-select="{{ opts.confirmOnSelect }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if labels.meridiem %} data-lily-date-time-picker-meridiem-label="{{ labels.meridiem }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.attributes %}{% for k, v in opts.attributes %} {{ k }}="{{ v }}"{% endfor %}{% endif %}
>
<input type="hidden" name="{{ name }}" value="{{ opts.value | default('') }}" data-lily-date-time-picker-hidden-input>

<div class="date-time-picker-field">
  <input
    class="date-time-picker-input"
    id="{{ fieldId }}"
    type="text"
    autocomplete="off"
    value="{{ opts.value | default('') }}"
    {%- if opts.placeholder %} placeholder="{{ opts.placeholder }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if opts.disabled %} disabled{% endif %}
    {%- if opts.readonly %} readonly{% endif %}
    {%- if opts.required %} required{% endif %}
    {%- if opts.describedBy %} aria-describedby="{{ opts.describedBy }}"{% endif %}
    data-lily-date-time-picker-input
  >
  <button
    type="button"
    class="date-time-picker-button"
    aria-label="{{ opts.label }}"
    aria-haspopup="dialog"
    aria-expanded="false"
    aria-controls="{{ dialogId }}"
    {%- if opts.disabled or opts.readonly %} disabled{% endif %}
    data-lily-date-time-picker-button
  >
{%- if caller %}{{ caller() }}{% else %}<span class="date-time-picker-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128197;&#65038;</span>{% endif -%}
  </button>
</div>

<div
  class="date-time-picker-dialog"
  id="{{ dialogId }}"
  role="dialog"
  aria-modal="true"
  aria-label="{{ opts.label }}"
  tabindex="-1"
  hidden
  data-lily-date-time-picker-dialog
>
{%- if usesDate %}
  <div class="date-time-picker-header">
    <button type="button" class="date-time-picker-previous-year" aria-label="{{ labels.previousYear }}" data-lily-date-time-picker-previous-year><span aria-hidden="true">&#171;</span></button>
    <button type="button" class="date-time-picker-previous-month" aria-label="{{ labels.previousMonth }}" data-lily-date-time-picker-previous-month><span aria-hidden="true">&#8249;</span></button>
    <span class="date-time-picker-period" id="{{ periodId }}" aria-live="polite" data-lily-date-time-picker-period></span>
    <button type="button" class="date-time-picker-next-month" aria-label="{{ labels.nextMonth }}" data-lily-date-time-picker-next-month><span aria-hidden="true">&#8250;</span></button>
    <button type="button" class="date-time-picker-next-year" aria-label="{{ labels.nextYear }}" data-lily-date-time-picker-next-year><span aria-hidden="true">&#187;</span></button>
  </div>
  <table class="date-time-picker-calendar" role="grid" aria-labelledby="{{ periodId }}" data-lily-date-time-picker-calendar>
    <thead><tr data-lily-date-time-picker-weekdays>
{%- if showWeekNumbers %}<th class="date-time-picker-week-heading" scope="col" abbr="{{ labels.week }}">{{ labels.week }}</th>{% endif -%}
    </tr></thead>
    <tbody data-lily-date-time-picker-grid></tbody>
  </table>
{%- endif %}

{%- if usesTime %}
  <div class="date-time-picker-time" data-lily-date-time-picker-time>
    <label class="date-time-picker-time-label" for="{{ hourId }}">{{ labels.hour }}</label>
    <select class="date-time-picker-hour" id="{{ hourId }}" data-lily-date-time-picker-hour></select>
    <label class="date-time-picker-time-label" for="{{ minuteId }}">{{ labels.minute }}</label>
    <select class="date-time-picker-minute" id="{{ minuteId }}" data-lily-date-time-picker-minute></select>
  </div>
{%- endif %}

  <div class="date-time-picker-shortcuts" data-lily-date-time-picker-shortcuts>
{%- for shortcut in shortcuts %}
    <button type="button" class="date-time-picker-shortcut" data-shortcut-id="{{ shortcut.id }}"{% if shortcut.days is defined %} data-days="{{ shortcut.days }}"{% endif %}{% if shortcut.months is defined %} data-months="{{ shortcut.months }}"{% endif %}{% if shortcut.date %} data-date="{{ shortcut.date }}"{% endif %}>{{ shortcut.label }}</button>
{%- endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="date-time-picker-footer">
{%- if labels.clear %}
    <button type="button" class="date-time-picker-clear" data-lily-date-time-picker-clear>{{ labels.clear }}</button>
{%- endif %}
    <button type="button" class="date-time-picker-cancel" data-lily-date-time-picker-cancel>{{ labels.cancel }}</button>
    <button type="button" class="date-time-picker-confirm" data-lily-date-time-picker-confirm>{{ labels.confirm }}</button>
  </div>
</div>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}
